Validity Criteria
- Blank control OD must be not more than 0.2;
- OD coefficient of variation of the standard reference at 2.5 μg/mL must be not more than 30%;
- The average of OD of the standard reference must be greater or equal to the average of the blank +3 standard deviation determined historically (e.g. 0.116 for FHA in solution);

- Both the 2 individual OD of sample must be less than or greater than the average OD of the standard reference at 2.5 μg/mL.
- OD of the sample must be less than or equal than the OD of the standard at 2.5 μg/mL divided by 2.

